&Q000660 = A song of Inana and Dumuzid (Dumuzid-Inana D1)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.4.08.30
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.4.08.30&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. [e₂]-temen-ni₂#-guru₃#-a# X [...]
#tr.en: The …… of @wTN{E-temen-ni-guru},
#lem: Etemenniguru[1]TN; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. e₂ %e uru₂-ze₂-ba %s šu si sa₂-a-bi
#tr.en: the organisation of the house of @wSN{Eridug},
#lem: e[house]; Uruzeb[1]SN; šu[hand]; si[horn]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. e₂ {d}suen-na-ka dadag-ga-bi
#tr.en: the radiance of the house of @wDN{Suen},
#lem: e[house]; Suen[1]DN; dadag[bright]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. e₂-an-na-ka urin du₃-a-bi
#tr.en: and the erected banners of the @wTN{E-ana} were
#lem: Eanak[1]TN; urin[standard]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. e₂ šu-bi-še₃ he₂-rig₇
#tr.en: all given as gifts to the house.
#lem: e[house]; šu[hand]; rig[donate]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. e₂ zid-da-ŋu₁₀ dungu-gen₆{du-gu-ge} i-im-dirig
#tr.en: My good house floats like a cloud;
#lem: e[house]; zid[right]; dungu[cloud]; dirig[make more than]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. mu inim-ŋar sag₉-ga in-ga-am₃
#tr.en: its name too is a favourable omen.
#lem: mu[name]; iŋar[oracular utterance]; sag[good]; me[be]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. ki-nu₂ gi-rin{ri}-na za-gin₃ sig₁₀{zi}-ga-am₃
#tr.en: He who excels at the ceremonies of queenship has lined with his straw the flowered couch,
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; girim[flower]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; sig[put into]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. {d}gibil₆ iri₁₂-gal-la mu-ra-an-kug-kug-ga
#tr.en: inlaid with lapis lazuli,
#lem: Gibil[1]DN; Irigal[1]TN; kug[purify]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. %e mu-lu₂ nam-ga-ša-an-e %s šu gal du₃-a
#tr.en: which @wDN{Gibil} has purified for you in the @wTN{Iri-gal} shrine and,
#lem: mulu[person]N; naŋgašan[ladyship]N; šu[hand]; gal[big]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. %e šu!(U₃)-mu-un-na-ni %s mu-ra-an-sig₉
#tr.en: in the house which he has sanctified for you with his sweet reeds,
#lem: šumun[grass]; sig[put into]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. e₂ {gi}ušub-na mu-ra-ab-kug-ga šu-luh mu-ra-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#tr.en: he is performing the purification rites for you.
#lem: e[house]; ušub[part of a reed]; kug[purify]; šuluh[ritual cleansing]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. ud ba-an-nu₂ ud ba-an-dug₄
#tr.en: On the day of the moon's disappearance,
#lem: ud[sun]; nud[lie down]; ud[sun]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. ud ki-nu₂-a %e i-bi₂ %s kar₂-kar₂-dam
#tr.en: the day appointed (?),
#lem: ud[sun]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; ibi[eye]N; kar[blow]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. ud %e u₃-mu-un-e %s mi₂ zi-zi-i-dam
#tr.en: the day when the couch will be inspected,
#lem: ud[sun]; umun[lord]N; mi[cvne]; zig[rise]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. %e u₃-mu-un-ra %s nam-til₃ ze₂-eŋ₃-ŋa₂-a
#tr.en: the day when the lord will make love,
#lem: umun[lord]N; namtil[life]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. %e u₃-mu-un-ra %s ešgiri₂ ($erroneous gloss si-bi-ir$) šibir šum₂{šu}-mu-na-ab
#tr.en: grant life to the lord and give the staff and the crook to the lord!
#lem: umun[lord]N; ešgiri[staff]; šibir[shepherd's staff]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. al ba-an-dug₄ al ba-an-dug₄ ki-nu₂ al ba-an-dug₄
#tr.en: She desires it, she desires it, she desires the couch.
#lem: al[cvne]; dug[speak]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. ki-nu₂ šag₄ hul₂-la al ba-an-dug₄ ki-nu₂ al ba-an-dug₄
#tr.en: She desires the couch of heart's joy, she desires the couch.
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; šag[heart]; hul[rejoice]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. ki-nu₂ ur₂ %e ze₂-ba %s al ba-an-dug₄ ki-nu₂ al ba-an-dug₄
#tr.en: She desires the couch of the sweet embrace, she desires the couch.
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; ur[loin]; zeb[good]V/i; al[cvne]; dug[speak]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. ki#-nu₂ nam-lugal-la al ba-an-dug₄ ki-nu₂ al ba-an-dug₄
#tr.en: She desires the kingly couch, she desires the couch.
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; namlugal[kingship]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. [ki]-nu₂ nam-nin-a al ba-an-dug₄ ki-nu₂ al ba-an-dug₄
#tr.en: She desires the queenly couch, she desires the couch.
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; namnin[ladyship]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; al[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. %e [ze₂]-ba#-ni-da ze₂-ba-ni-da %s ki-nu₂ %e ze₂-ba-ni-da
#tr.en: When she makes comfortable, when she makes comfortable, when she makes the couch comfortable; when she makes the couch of heart's joy comfortable, when she makes the couch comfortable; when she makes the couch of the sweet embrace comfortable, when she makes the couch comfortable; when she makes the kingly couch comfortable, when she makes the couch comfortable; when she makes the queenly couch comfortable, when she makes the couch comfortable,
#lem: zeb[good]V/i; zeb[good]V/i; kinud[sleeping quarter]; zeb[good]V/i
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. [ki-nu₂] šag₄ hul₂-la %e ze₂-ba-ni-da %s ki-nu₂ %e ze₂-ba-ni-da
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; šag[heart]; hul[rejoice]; zeb[good]V/i; kinud[sleeping quarter]; zeb[good]V/i
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. [ki-nu₂] ur₂# %e ze₂-ba ze₂-ba-ni-da %s ki-nu₂ %e ze₂-ba-ni-da
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; ur[loin]; zeb[good]V/i; zeb[good]V/i; kinud[sleeping quarter]; zeb[good]V/i
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. [ki-nu₂] nam#-lugal-la %e ze₂-ba-ni-da %s ki-nu₂ %e ze₂-ba-ni-da
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; namlugal[kingship]; zeb[good]V/i; kinud[sleeping quarter]; zeb[good]V/i
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. [ki-nu₂ nam]-nin-a %e ze₂-ba-ni-da %s ki-nu₂ %e ze₂-ba-ni-da
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; namnin[ladyship]; zeb[good]V/i; kinud[sleeping quarter]; zeb[good]V/i
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. [X X ki]-nu₂# mu-un-na-barag₂-ge ki-nu₂ mu-un-na-barag₂-ge
#tr.en: she covers the couch for him ……, covers the couch for him;
#lem: X; X; kinud[sleeping quarter]; barag[spread out]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; barag[spread out]
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. [X X ki-nu₂ mu]-un#-na-barag₂-ge ki-nu₂ mu-un-na-barag₂-ge
#tr.en: she covers the couch for him ……, covers the couch for him;
#lem: X; X; kinud[sleeping quarter]; barag[spread out]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; barag[spread out]
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. lugal# [ki-nu₂ %e ze₂-ba-ni-še₃ %s gu₃ mu-un-na-de₂-e]
#tr.en: she calls the king to her sweet couch,
#lem: lugal[king]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; zeb[good]V/i; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. ki aŋ₂ ki-nu₂# %e ze₂-ba-ni-še₃# %s gu₃# mu-un#-[na-de₂-e]
#tr.en: she calls the beloved to her sweet couch,
#lem: ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; kinud[sleeping quarter]; zeb[good]V/i; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. inim{i-ni} til₃ inim ud su₁₃-ra₂{ra} gu₃ mu-un-na-de₂-e
#tr.en: and speaks to him words of life, words of long days.
#lem: inim[word]; til[live (of a single person)]; inim[word]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#etcsl: line-id=32

33.  %e  ga-ša-an-šubur-ra  %s  sukkal zid e₂-an-na-ke₄
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninšubur}, the good minister of @wTN{E-ana}, clasps him by his right hand and brings him in bliss to @wDN{Inana's} embrace:
#lem: Gašanšubur[1]DN; sukkal[secretary]; zid[right]; Eanak[1]TN
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. kišib-la₂!{ki-še-eb-la₂} zid-da-na im-ma-an-dab₅
#tr.en: @q[Nincubur,Inana]{“May the lord whom you have chosen in your heart,
#lem: kišibla[wrist]; zid[right]; dab[seize]
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. ur₂ %e ga-ša-an-na-ka-še₃ %s hi-li-a mu-ni-kur₉
#tr.en: the king, your beloved husband,
#lem: ur[loin]; Gašanana[1]DN; hili[attractiveness]; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. %e u₃-mu-un-e aŋ₂ %s šag₄-ge ba-e-pad₃-da-zu
#tr.en: enjoy long days in your holy and sweet embrace!
#lem: umun[lord]N; aŋ[thing]N; šag[heart]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. lugal-e nitalam ki aŋ₂-zu ur₂ kug niŋ₂ dug₃-zu ud ha-ba-ni-ib-su₃-ud-de₃
#tr.en: Give him a propitious and famous reign,
#lem: lugal[king]; ŋidlam[(equal ranking) spouse]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; ur[loin]; kug[purify]; niŋ[thing]; dug[good]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]
#etcsl: line-id=37

38. bal sag₉-ga pa e₃ šum₂-mu-un-ab
#tr.en: give him a royal throne of kingship on its firm foundation,
#lem: bala[turn]; sag[good]; pa[branch]; e[leave]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. {ŋiš}gu-za nam-lugal-la suhuš gen₆-na-ba šum₂-mu-na-ab
#tr.en: give him the sceptre to guide the Land, and the staff and crook,
#lem: guza[chair]; namlugal[kingship]; suhuš[foundation]; gin[confirm]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. ŋidru kalam si sa₂ ešgiri₂ šibir šum₂-mu-na-ab
#tr.en: and give him the righteous headdress and the crown which glorifies the head!
#lem: ŋidru[scepter]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; ešgiri[staff]; šibir[shepherd's staff]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. aga zid men-na saŋ dalla-a šum₂-mu-na-ab
#tr.en: From the rising of the sun to the setting of the sun,
#lem: aga[tiara]; zid[right]; men[tiara]; saŋ[head]; dalla[(to be) bright]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. {d}utu e₃-ta {d}utu šu₂-še₃
#tr.en: from the south to the north,
#lem: Utu[1]DN; e[leave]; Utu[1]DN; šuš[cover]
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. {tum₉}ulu₃-ta{tu-mu-ul-lu-ta} {tum₉}mir-ra-a-še₃{tu-mu-{d}mi-ra}
#tr.en: from the upper sea to the lower sea,
#lem: ulu[south wind]; mir[north wind]
#etcsl: line-id=43

44. a-ab-ba igi-nim-ta a-ab-ba sig-še₃
#tr.en: from where the @fsux{ḫalub} tree grows to where the cedar grows,
#lem: aʾabak[sea]; iginim[upper land]; aʾabak[sea]; sig[weak]
#etcsl: line-id=44

45. {ŋiš}ha-lu-ub₂!-ta {ŋiš}erin-na-še₃!(TA)
#tr.en: over all @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad},
#lem: halub[tree]; eren[cedar]
#etcsl: line-id=45

46. ki-en-gi ki-uri-a ešgiri₂ šibir šum₂-mu-na-ab!(TA)
#tr.en: grant him the staff and the crook!”}
#lem: Kengir[1]; Akkad[1 Akkad]; ešgiri[staff]; šibir[shepherd's staff]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=46

47. saŋ gig₂ dur₂-ru-na-bi nam-sipad-bi he₂-ak-e
#tr.en: @q{“May he act as shepherd of the black-headed inhabitants;
#lem: saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; durun[sit]; namsipad[shepherdship]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=47

48. e-ne engar-gin₇ gana₂ he₂-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#tr.en: may he, like a farmer, make the fields productive;
#lem: ane[he]; engar[farmer]; gana[field]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=48

49. sipad zid-gin₇ amaš he₂-em-mi-lu-lu
#tr.en: may he make the sheepfolds multiply, like a trustworthy shepherd.
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; amaš[sheepfold]; lu[abundant]
#etcsl: line-id=49

50. gu he₂-en-da-ŋal₂ še he₂-en-da-ŋal₂
#tr.en: Under him, may there be flax, may there be barley;
#lem: gu[cord]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; še[barley]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=50

51. id₂-da a-eštub he₂-en-da-ŋal₂
#tr.en: in the rivers may there be carp floods. Under him,
#lem: id[river]; aʾeštub[early flooding]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=51

52. a-šag₄-ga še gu-nu he₂-en-da-ŋal₂
#tr.en: may there be mottled barley in the fields;
#lem: ašag[field]; še[barley]; gunu[qualification of barley]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=52

53. ambar-ra ku₆ mušen gu₃ hu-mu-da-ra-ra
#tr.en: in the marshes, fish, and may the birds chatter.
#lem: ambar[reed-bed]; kud[fish]; mušen[bird]; gu[voice]; rah[beat]
#etcsl: line-id=53

54. %e mu-gi-e %s gi sumun gi henbur he₂-en-da-an-mu₂
#tr.en: Under him, may the old reeds and the young reeds grow tall in the reedbeds;
#lem: mugi[thicket]; gi[reed]; sumun[old]; gi[reed]; henbur[stalk]; mu[grow]
#etcsl: line-id=54

55. an-edin-na %e {mu}maš-gurum %s he₂-en-da-an-mu₂
#tr.en: under him, may the @fsux{mašgurum} bushes flourish on the high plains.
#lem: aneden[the high steppe]; mašgurum[plant]; mu[grow]
#etcsl: line-id=55

56. tir-tir-ra šeg₉ šeg₉-bar he₂-en-da-lu
#tr.en: Under him, may the wild sheep and wild goats multiply in the forests;
#lem: tir[forest]; šeg[an animal]; šeŋbar[an animal]; lu[abundant]
#etcsl: line-id=56

57. pu₂-{ŋiš}kiri₆ lal₃ ŋeštin he₂-en-da-il₂
#tr.en: under him, may the irrigated orchards produce syrup and wine.
#lem: pukiri[irrigated orchard]; lal[syrup]; ŋeštin[vine]; il[raise]
#etcsl: line-id=57

58. mu₂-sar-ra hi-iz{sar} za₃-hi-li{sar} he₂-en-da-mu₂
#tr.en: Under him, may lettuce and cress flourish in the garden plots;
#lem: musar[garden]; hiz[vegetable]; zahili[plant]; mu[grow]
#etcsl: line-id=58

59. e₂-gal-la zi su₃-ud-ŋal₂ he₂-en-da-an-ŋal₂
#tr.en: under him, may there be long life in the palace.”}
#lem: egal[palace]; zi[life]; sudŋal[long-lasting]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=59

60. {id₂}idigna {id₂}buranun-na a-u₅-ba hu-mu-ni-ib-tum₂#
#tr.en: @q{“May high flood-waters flow in the @wWN{Tigris} and @wWN{Euphrates}, may the grasses grow tall on their banks,
#lem: Idigna[1 Tigris]; Buranun[1 Euphrates]; aʾu[high water]; tum[bring]
#etcsl: line-id=60

61. gu₂-gu₂-ba u₂ hu-mu-ta-mu₂-mu₂ a-gar₃ he₂-en-si
#tr.en: and may the meadows be covered.
#lem: gu[neck]; u[plant(s)]; mu[grow]; agar[meadow]; si[fill]
#etcsl: line-id=61

62. guru₇-du₆ guru₇-maš kug %e ga-ša-an %s {d}nisaba-ke₄ gu₂ hu-mu-ni-gur-gur
#tr.en: May the holy lady @wDN{Nisaba} pile high the grain heaps and mounds.
#lem: gurudud[grain heap]; gurumaš[grain heap]; kug[purify]; gašan[lady]N; Nisabak[1]DN; gu[neck]; gur[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=62

63. %e ga-ša-an-ŋu₁₀# %s nin an ki nin an ki šu₂-a
#tr.en: My lady, queen of heaven and earth, queen who encompasses heaven and earth,
#lem: gašan[lady]N; nin[lady]; an[sky]; ki[place]; nin[lady]; an[sky]; ki[place]; šuš[cover]
#etcsl: line-id=63

64. ur₂ [...] ud ha-ba-ni-ib-sud-e
#tr.en: may he enjoy long days …… embrace.”}
#lem: ur[loin]; X; ud[sun]; sud[distant]
#etcsl: line-id=64

65. lugal [...] saŋ# il₂-la mu-un-ŋen-ne₂
#tr.en: With head high,
#lem: lugal[king]; X; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=65

66. ur₂ kug# [%e ga-ša-an-na]-ka#-še₃ %s saŋ il₂-la mu-un-ŋen
#tr.en: the king goes now ……,
#lem: ur[loin]; kug[purify]; Gašanana[1]DN; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=66

67. lugal X [... saŋ] il₂#-la ŋen-ne₂
#tr.en: with head high he goes to the holy embrace of @wDN{Inana}.
#lem: lugal[king]; X; X; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=67

68. nin!-ŋu₁₀-[ra] saŋ# il₂-la ŋen-ne₂
#tr.en: The king going now with head high ……,
#lem: nin[lady]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=68

69. X U₃ [...] il₂-la KA-ta
#tr.en: going now to my lady with head high, @gap{1 line fragmentary} he embraces the mistress.
